    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19503" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾰρύ̆-τονος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόνος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>deep-sounding,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. φωνεῖν,</span> of dogs, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Phgn.</u>
				813b2
			</span></i>; so prob. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. στῆθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					5.30
				</span></i>
			; <i>deep,</i> of musical notes, <i><span class="en">
				Bacch.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Gramm., of
			enclitics, <i>unaccented,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				35.25
			</span></i>; of words, <i>not oxytone,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				38.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				674.18
			</span></i>, etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1012
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				16.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				41.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Moer.
				109
			</span></i>.</div>
